    "text": {
     "en": "The period between the wars (1919-1939) saw big changes. The Russian Revolution of 1917 under Lenin set up a communist state, and Stalin later led the Soviet Union through planned development.\nIn 1929 the Great Depression began with the stock market crash in the USA. Banks failed and many lost jobs. President Roosevelt's New Deal tried to revive the economy.\nDictators rose in Europe: Mussolini's fascism in Italy and Hitler's Nazism in Germany. Japan expanded in Asia. These aggressive regimes and the failure of the League of Nations led to war."
    }
